{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-action-unique","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:categorical-action-unique","kind":"proposition","title":"Uniqueness of the categorical action (given $\\Phi$)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-action-exists"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-action-unique"],"tags":["uniqueness","categorical-action"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalAction.unique","text":"categorical-action-unique.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action-unique.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:categorical-action-unique\"></a><p>For a fixed Lagrangian endomorphism <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi \\in \\mathrm{End}_{\\mathbf{C}}(A)</code>, the categorical action <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{S}_\\Phi = \\mathrm{tr}(\\Phi)</code> is uniquely determined. Any morphism <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{1} \\to \\mathbf{1}</code> factoring as <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{ev}_A \\circ (\\mathrm{id}_{A^\\vee} \\otimes \\Phi) \\circ \\mathrm{coev}_A</code> equals <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{tr}(\\Phi)</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action-unique.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"3.13.3"}
